<section id="view-loading" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-loading">
<p class="view-intro">Build a company roster, review the names, then start collection.</p>
<div id="roster-panel" class="loading-grid"><div class="panel roster-editor">
<div class="section-label">01 · BUILD YOUR ROSTER</div><h2>Sector & companies</h2>
<form id="roster-form">
<label class="field" for="sector">Sector</label><input id="sector" type="text" maxlength="31" placeholder="e.g. Credit unions, Community banks" required autocomplete="off">
<p class="muted">Use each company’s canonical name once. Add other names below.</p>
<div id="company-editor"></div>
<div class="editor-actions"><button id="add-company" type="button" class="secondary">+ Add company</button><button id="review-roster" type="submit" class="primary">Review roster</button></div>
<p id="draft-status" class="muted" role="status">Draft stays in this browser.</p>
</form>
<details class="file-import"><summary>Or upload a spreadsheet</summary>
<label class="upload" for="file"><strong>Choose a roster</strong><span>CSV, TSV, or Excel · up to 5 MB</span><input id="file" type="file" accept=".csv,.tsv,.xlsx"></label>
<a class="text-link" href="/template.csv" download="mentat-roster-template.csv">Download the upload template ↗</a>
<p>Use <code>canonical_name</code>, <code>alias</code>, and <code>sector</code> columns. Repeat the canonical name for each alias. <code>industry</code> is also accepted. Optional: <code>exclusion</code>. Mentat’s existing roster workbooks work too.</p></details>
</div><div class="panel launch-panel"><div class="section-label">02 · REVIEW & COLLECT</div><h2>Collection setup</h2>
<p id="review-placeholder">Review your roster to see the exact names that will be searched. No data collection starts until you press Start collection.</p>
<div id="upload-review" hidden><h3>Roster review</h3><div id="roster-counts"></div><div id="roster-list"></div>
<fieldset><legend>Election cycles</legend><label><input type="checkbox" name="cycle" value="2022" checked> 2021–22</label><label><input type="checkbox" name="cycle" value="2024" checked> 2023–24</label><label><input type="checkbox" name="cycle" value="2026" checked> 2025–26</label></fieldset>
<label class="field" for="api-key">FEC API key <span id="key-hint">Saved encrypted for your Windows account. Separate multiple keys with commas.</span></label><input id="api-key" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Enter your API key">
<button id="save-keys" type="button" class="secondary">Save keys securely</button><button id="start" type="button" class="primary" disabled>Start collection</button></div>
<p id="key-status" class="local-note"></p>
<p class="local-note">Closing the browser does not stop collection. Follow checkpoints and incoming records in the Collection tab.</p></div></div>
<section class="panel coverage-panel" aria-labelledby="loading-coverage-title"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 id="loading-coverage-title">Saved FEC coverage</h2><details class="inline-help"><summary>How coverage is assessed</summary><p>Coverage applies to the saved run’s roster and searches. Review changed company names and aliases before reusing it. An active cycle is flagged stale when its verified cutoff is more than 30 days behind today; a past cycle requires coverage through December 31.</p></details></div><div id="loading-coverage" role="status"><p>Unverifiable · Checking saved coverage evidence.</p></div></section>
</section>
<section id="view-collection" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-collection" hidden>
<div class="run-library"><div class="run-collections" role="group" aria-label="Collection folders"><button type="button" data-run-group="progress" aria-pressed="true">In progress <span id="run-count-progress">0</span></button><button type="button" data-run-group="history" aria-pressed="false">History <span id="run-count-history">0</span></button><button type="button" data-run-group="archived" aria-pressed="false">Archived <span id="run-count-archived">0</span></button></div><div class="run-toolbar"><label for="runs">Collection<select id="runs"><option value="">No collections yet</option></select></label><button id="archive-run" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Archive run</button></div><p id="run-library-note" class="muted"></p><details class="working-folders"><summary>Working folders</summary><p><strong>Collection work &amp; checkpoints</strong><br><span id="collection-directory"></span></p><p><strong>Completed reports</strong><br><span id="completed-directory"></span></p><button id="view-completed-reports" type="button" class="secondary">View completed reports</button></details></div>
<h2 id="run-title" class="run-heading">Your collection workspace</h2>
<button id="resume-setup" type="button" class="secondary" hidden>Continue collection setup</button>
<p id="run-readiness-note" class="muted" hidden></p>
<div id="empty" class="empty"><div class="empty-mark">M</div><h3>Start with a list of names.</h3><p>Your companies, collection checkpoints, and incoming records will appear here. You can also inspect an existing run from the list.</p></div>
<div id="monitor" hidden>
<p id="freshness" class="muted"></p>

<div class="quality-panel" role="status"><strong id="quality-title">Collection coverage unverified</strong><p id="quality-detail">Completed tasks do not establish complete downstream coverage.</p><div id="quality-checks"></div><button id="clear-quality" type="button" hidden>Clear reviewed notices</button><details><summary>Data scope and source age</summary><p>Search checks cover the requested names at collection time. Missing employer names and unlisted aliases can still leave gaps. Rebuilt reports show observed committee transfers through three hops, with unresolved paths and separate conditional estimates. These are not traced company dollars or lower bounds. Historical reports may predate transfer coverage.</p><p>Rebuilt reports classify ActBlue and WinRed as hybrid/Carey committees. Older exports may still use the former Super PAC reporting rule.</p><ul id="source-snapshots"></ul></details></div>
<div id="run-controls"><div class="section-label">RUN CONTROLS</div><div class="editor-actions"><button id="stop" type="button" class="danger" disabled title="No collection is running">Stop collection</button><label class="field" for="worker-target">Workers</label><input id="worker-target" type="number" min="1" max="64" placeholder="e.g. 6" disabled title="No collection is running"><button id="apply-workers" type="button" class="secondary" disabled title="No collection is running">Apply</button></div></div>
<div class="metrics"><div><span>Search tasks processed</span><strong id="completed">—</strong></div><div><span id="worker-metric-label">Active workers</span><strong id="workers">—</strong><small id="worker-detail"></small></div><div><span>Failed tasks</span><strong id="failed">—</strong></div><div><span>Estimated time left</span><strong id="eta">—</strong><small>Elapsed <span id="elapsed">—</span></small></div></div>
<span id="stopping-banner" class="badge" hidden>Stopping - finishing in-flight lanes.</span>
<div class="progress-track"><div id="progress"></div></div><p id="phase-description" class="muted"></p>
<div id="industries" class="industry-list"></div>
<section class="panel coverage-panel" aria-labelledby="collection-coverage-title"><div class="panel-heading"><h2 id="collection-coverage-title">FEC data-through by sector and cycle</h2><details class="inline-help"><summary>How coverage is assessed</summary><p>Dated evidence must cover every company’s employer and corporate searches. Task completion, retrieval time and file modification time do not establish a cutoff. Active cycles allow a 30-day lag; past cycles require coverage through December 31.</p></details></div><div id="collection-coverage" role="status"></div></section>
<div id="worker-panel" class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><h3>Collection workers</h3><label for="lanes">Inspect worker <select id="lanes"><option>No workers yet</option></select></label></div><div id="lane-summary" class="muted">Waiting for collection to start.</div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Cycle</th><th>Search</th><th>Rows fetched</th><th>Source count</th><th>Checkpoint</th></tr></thead><tbody id="checkpoints"></tbody></table></div></div>
<div id="records-panel" class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><h3>Activity Log</h3><p class="muted">Latest 25 stored records from the selected worker. Provisional until reconciliation and coverage checks finish. Positions use reported titles until final report classification.</p></div><span class="badge subtle">RAW DATA</span></div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Person</th><th class="number">Amount</th><th>Position</th><th>Title</th><th>Recipient</th></tr></thead><tbody id="records"></tbody></table></div></div>
<div class="bottom-grid"><div class="panel"><h3>Run events</h3><div id="events" class="events"></div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Completed reports</h3><div id="reports"><p class="muted">Reports appear after collection and validation succeed.</p></div></div></div>
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="report-freshness-title"><h3 id="report-freshness-title">Report freshness</h3><p>Retrieval records when a source was downloaded. Modification records a file change. Only an explicit verified data-through date describes coverage; unknown means the receipts do not establish it.</p><div id="report-freshness"></div></section>
</div></section>
<section id="view-cross-reference" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-cross-reference" hidden>
<p class="xref-intro">One coherent account of who supplied the money and where it went. Mentat cross-references FEC evidence automatically, preserves each decision, and brings unresolved cases forward for review.</p>
<div class="xref-toolbar"><button id="xref-refresh" type="button" class="secondary">Refresh saved evidence</button><span id="xref-refresh-status" role="status">Read-only · Refreshes every 5 seconds while this tab is visible.</span></div>
<div id="xref-results"><p class="muted">Loading the latest cross-reference evidence…</p></div>
</section>
<script src="/cross-reference.js" defer></script>
<section id="view-graph" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-graph" hidden>
<section class="panel graph-controls" aria-label="Scope">
<div class="scope-heading"><span class="section-label">SCOPE</span><div class="scope-actions"><details class="report-location"><summary>Report folder</summary><label for="graph-run">Source folder<select id="graph-run"></select></label></details><button id="graph-reset" type="button" class="graph-text-button">Reset</button></div></div>
