<div class="panel-heading"><div><div class="section-label">FOLLOW THE REPORTED MONEY</div><h2>Company → PAC → candidates</h2><p>Explore the recorded legs. Spending from a pooled PAC is committee activity; it cannot be assigned to a particular donor without further evidence.</p></div></div>
<div class="evidence-toolbar"><label for="evidence-cycle">Election cycle<select id="evidence-cycle"></select></label><label for="evidence-committee">Spending committee<select id="evidence-committee"></select></label></div>
<p id="evidence-scope" class="muted"></p><div id="evidence-funding" class="evidence-cards"></div>
<div id="evidence-transfers"></div>
<div class="allocation-panel"><h3>Conditional company cash estimate</h3><div id="allocation-status" role="status"></div><div id="allocation-results"></div><details><summary>Estimation method &amp; assumptions</summary><p>At each payment, assign the same fraction as the company's share of the PAC's available cash. Carry that fraction through PAC transfers; leave retained cash and operating expenses in their own categories.</p><p class="formula">Estimated company-funded spending = payment × company cash share before payment</p><p class="muted">Example only: a 25% cash share × $10 million of candidate spending gives a $2.5 million estimate. This is an accounting assumption, not proof of donor intent or influence.</p></details></div>
<details><summary>Company receipt evidence and excluded conversions</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Reported name / role</th><th>Date</th><th>Amount</th><th>Filing explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody id="evidence-receipts"></tbody></table></div></details>
<h3 class="evidence-subheading">Candidate activity as filed</h3><p class="muted">Amounts below belong to the selected committee. Support and opposition stay separate. Expand a name to compare the filing with the candidate register.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Candidate / identity check</th><th>Direction</th><th class="number">Committee spending</th><th class="number">Estimated company funding</th><th>Activity dates</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody id="evidence-candidates"></tbody></table></div>
<details><summary>What is needed for a donor allocation?</summary><p>Reconcile all receipts and disbursements, opening and retained cash, asset conversions and refunds. Enforce donation → transfer → expenditure dates, including transfers between cycles. Document any earmark before calling a dollar amount traced. Otherwise, show assumptions and uncertainty with the estimate.</p><p id="evidence-timing" class="muted"></p></details>
</section>
